ss=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Squee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/839576-onyx-path-s-scion-2nd-edition?p=841224#post841224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This makes me happy, Neall. It's nice to see that there's faith (pardon the pun) in the line, and some longevity planned. It's nice to know that we'll be throwing questions at you for a long time to come <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And money. Don't forget money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T16:16:53-08:00","id":841557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/839576-onyx-path-s-scion-2nd-edition?p=840776#post840776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, it's an unlimited line. We'll keep writing books as long as you keep buyin' 'em, or until we run out of quality ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, I'd like to point out World of Darkness: Gypsy as proof that just because you run out of good idea's, doesn't mean that you have to stop writing *lol*<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-03T22:43:14-08:00","id":841736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/839576-onyx-path-s-scion-2nd-edition?p=840383#post840383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, will this also leave room for growth. For example the possibility of Pantheon books that include things like lesser known gods that you can play the children of, pantheon specific boons for purviews, birthrights that are more specifically targeted at that particular pantheon, and titanspawn that may face THAT specific pantheon more often. As well as stats for the gods, because as I told my buddy &quot;This is a game where you will need to have the Gods Stat'd out, because you JUST MIGHT have to fight them.<br /> <br /> Or is this going to be like White Wolf's version, a limited run. If so that will make me a sad panda</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/839576-onyx-path-s-scion-2nd-edition?p=840798#post840798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">are there any plans for having books that go really deep into the details of each individual pantheon like ragnarok did with the norse?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't really matter but I though I would selfishly note the existence of the Ask Neall thread...mostly because I dont want to have to look in two places to see these great questions answered lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T01:32:38-08:00","id":841782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/839576-onyx-path-s-scion-2nd-edition?p=840383#post840383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or is this going to be like White Wolf's version, a limited run. If so that will make me a sad panda</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider from a purely practical standpoint:<br /> <br /> Scion and the Trinity Continuum are currently the only lines that Onyx Path owns 100%. (We share ownership of the Scarred Lands.) Everything else is effectively licensed.<br /> <br /> Let's say there's a great earthquake, the sun turns black like sackcloth, the whole moon turns blood red, and White Wolf cancels their licence with us. Scion and Trinity suddenly become a lot more vital to Onyx Path. These are Onyx Path's legs to stand on. Even with the WW license, we want Onyx Path to be more than just a WW-licensed outfit: It's more than that. Bigger. We're thrilled with how well Pugmire is doing, for example, despite that being another license.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the upshot is that Neall's right: we're in this for the long haul. Scion and the Trinity Continuum are very important to Onyx Path for a multitude of different reasons, and we plan to keep making them both for years to come, if you'll let us. We have a lot of ideas for both game lines which extend and expand them far beyond the boundaries of the original edition, and we're excited to share that vision with all of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T21:16:39-08:00","id":842396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/839576-onyx-path-s-scion-2nd-edition?p=839836#post839836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's probably a Warrior Knack.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Speaking of Knacks, I've been trying to come up with an idea for a <i>Delayed Reaction</i> type of ability.<br /> <br /> The concept behind it is that the character is able to perform a physical action, but the subject doesn't immediately seem affected by it. Kind of like the legends of somebody slicing a person in half, but it takes a few seconds before they fall to pieces. Just to name one example.<br /> <br /> Hard part is thinking up mechanics for it that would actually be useful in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T23:15:15-08:00","id":842425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/839576-onyx-path-s-scion-2nd-edition?p=842396#post842396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Speaking of Knacks, I've been trying to come up with an idea for a <i>Delayed Reaction</i> type of ability.<br /> <br /> The concept behind it is that the character is able to perform a physical action, but the subject doesn't immediately seem affected by it. Kind of like the legends of somebody slicing a person in half, but it takes a few seconds before they fall to pieces. Just to name one example.<br /> <br /> Hard part is thinking up mechanics for it that would actually be useful in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Simply have the knack, delay the mechanical and visual effects of the attack, until the targets next tick","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T08:21:14-07:00","id":846573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/839576-onyx-path-s-scion-2nd-edition?p=842396#post842396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Speaking of Knacks, I've been trying to come up with an idea for a <i>Delayed Reaction</i> type of ability.<br /> <br /> The concept behind it is that the character is able to perform a physical action, but the subject doesn't immediately seem affected by it. Kind of like the legends of somebody slicing a person in half, but it takes a few seconds before they fall to pieces. Just to name one example.<br /> <br /> Hard part is thinking up mechanics for it that would actually be useful in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just playing Devil's Advocate here, but couldn't that be replicated as a stunt alongside a task or action?<br /> <br /> Though, what would you want it to mechanically do beyond having a target stunned/awed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T11:50:16-07:00","id":846657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/839576-onyx-path-s-scion-2nd-edition?p=846573#post846573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Just playing Devil's Advocate here, but couldn't that be replicated as a stunt alongside a task or action?<br /> <br /> Though, what would you want it to mechanically do beyond having a target stunned/awed?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> One idea I had was it would allow for a surprise attack even if the enemy is aware of your presence. For example, they drop their guard, thinking the attack missed or failed, and then it takes effect when they aren't prepared for it.<br /> <br /> To refresh my memory, how long does a tick last? I want to say it's 6 seconds, but I could be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T14:02:31-07:00","id":846717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/839576-onyx-path-s-scion-2nd-edition?p=846657#post846657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> One idea I had was it would allow for a surprise attack even if the enemy is aware of your presence. For example, they drop their guard, thinking the attack missed or failed, and then it takes effect when they aren't prepared for it.<br /> <br /> To refresh my memory, how long does a tick last? I want to say it's 6 seconds, but I could be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be made as a Wits Knack, and the target fails a contested Perception+Awareness roll, then they cannot react for a full 5 ticks (the length of an instant action).<br /> <br /> As for the length of a tick, one tick = one second of time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T19:17:41-07:00","id":889559,"title":"","content":"For the KS, I know we're a ways off ...... but I'm really really really really hoping to see a few stretch goals allow us to add some additional pantheons to the book. I love the current set that is offered, don't get me wrong, but I would also love to see a few more make the cut (I'd love to see the Yazata be included. One of my favorites).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>in any fight<br /> it is the guy who is willing to die<br /> who is going to win that inch.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BlackRoleplayersOrganization\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/BlackRoleplayersOrganization</a>","edited":{"userid":1402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1402-kael-winters","user":"Kael Winters","date":". 05-12-2016, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1402-kael-winters","name":"Kael Winters","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1402_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T23:56:43-07:00","id":889709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kael Winters</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/839576-onyx-path-s-scion-2nd-edition?p=889559#post889559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the KS, I know we're a ways off ...... but I'm really really really really hoping to see a few stretch goals allow us to add some additional pantheons to the book. I love the current set that is offered, don't get me wrong, but I would also love to see a few more make the cut (I'd love to see the Yazata be included. One of my favorites).</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall's said he'd like to do pantheons as stretch goals, although they'd be supplements rather than additions to the books. The stretch goal pantheons would be the more difficult pantheons, ones that require more of a fictional flourish or different play from the default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T19:29:56-07:00","id":890346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/839576-onyx-path-s-scion-2nd-edition?p=889709#post889709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Neall's said he'd like to do pantheons as stretch goals, although they'd be supplements rather than additions to the books. The stretch goal pantheons would be the more difficult pantheons, ones that require more of a fictional flourish or different play from the default.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wouldn't mind a supplement of pantheons as a stretch goal. Just so long as I have a way of getting my Yazata <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Don't get me wrong, I love .... LOVE what is offered in the core ... Yazata will just make it all complete for me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>in any fight<br /> it is the guy who is willing to die<br /> who is going to win that inch.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BlackRoleplayersOrganization\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.facebook.com/BlackRoleplayersOrganization</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1402-kael-winters","name":"Kael Winters","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1402_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T06:15:19-07:00","id":893970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/839576-onyx-path-s-scion-2nd-edition?p=841782#post841782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Consider from a purely practical standpoint:<br /> <br /> Scion and the Trinity Continuum are currently the only lines that Onyx Path owns 100%. (We share ownership of the Scarred Lands.) Everything else is effectively licensed.<br /> <br /> Let's say there's a great earthquake, the sun turns black like sackcloth, the whole moon turns blood red, and White Wolf cancels their licence with us. Scion and Trinity suddenly become a lot more vital to Onyx Path. These are Onyx Path's legs to stand on. Even with the WW license, we want Onyx Path to be more than just a WW-licensed outfit: It's more than that. Bigger. We're thrilled with how well Pugmire is doing, for example, despite that being another license.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the upshot is that Neall's right: we're in this for the long haul. Scion and the Trinity Continuum are very important to Onyx Path for a multitude of different reasons, and we plan to keep making them both for years to come, if you'll let us. We have a lot of ideas for both game lines which extend and expand them far beyond the boundaries of the original edition, and we're excited to share that vision with all of you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I'm wrong, but Pugmire is owned by Eddy Webb, and Cavaliers of Mars is owned by Rose Bailey?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}